# AORT — Code Owners
#
# Routes review to the owner responsible for each module, per the work
# division in the project blueprint. Shared interfaces require both owners.
#
# Owner A — @kolursamith             digital twin, scenario semantics, AI,
#                                    recovery optimizer, decision logic
# Owner B — @girinandanv9845-ship-it banking, telemetry, AWS, infrastructure,
#                                    failure-injection infrastructure
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the shared default comes first
# and the more specific module rules below override it.
#
# NOTE: this file only takes effect once branch protection enables
# "Require review from Code Owners" on main and develop. See
# docs/branch-protection.md — a repo admin must apply those settings.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: anything not claimed below needs both owners.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                           @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner A — twin, scenario semantics, AI, optimizer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/digital-twin/              @kolursamith
/ai/                        @kolursamith
/optimizer/                 @kolursamith

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner B — banking workload, telemetry, cloud and infrastructure
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/banking/                   @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/telemetry/                 @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/aws/                       @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/infrastructure/            @girinandanv9845-ship-it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scenarios are split: Owner A owns scenario semantics and impact
# propagation; Owner B owns the failure-injection infrastructure that
# actually perturbs the running system.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/scenarios/                 @kolursamith
/scenarios/injection/       @girinandanv9845-ship-it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Joint ownership — shared interfaces and anything both owners depend on.
# Contracts in particular must never be changed by one owner alone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/contracts/                 @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/tests/                     @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/docs/                      @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/dashboard/                 @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it

# Repository governance itself is joint.
/.github/                   @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it
/AGENTS.md                  @kolursamith @girinandanv9845-ship-it
